  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile (0.650–0.653), while image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208). We have not yet tested whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) combined with the best RNA setup can improve upon the RNA-only baseline. This experiment (config_038: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, concat fusion) isolates the question of whether adding image features with a powerful pretrained ViT encoder provides complementary signal. Transformer aggregation was marginally preferred for scvi_n200 (0.653 vs 0.650), and concat is the simpler, more standard fusion choice. With only 2 experiments remaining after this one, testing the most promising multimodal combination now is critical: if it beats 0.653, we can fine-tune fusion type in the last experiments; if it does not, we confirm the RNA-only scvi_n200 + multiprofile configuration is optimal and avoid wasting budget on weaker multimodal variants."
}

